[E0436] Error: `n` is used after `right`, which it refers to, was changed
    ╭─[ err/429_an_alternatives_binding_holds_each_element/main.wip:14:16 ]
    │
 12 │         (.Some(n), _) | (_, .Some(n)) => {
    │                ┬
    │                ╰── `n` refers to `right`
 13 │             right = .None
    │             ──┬──
    │               ╰──── `right` assigned here
 14 │             io::println(n.toStr())
    │                         ┬
    │                         ╰── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `n` before `right` changes, or take what is needed from it before then
    │
    │ Note: a binding of a pattern on a place refers to the place, so the place must not change while the binding is still used
────╯
